563
00:41:17,745 --> 00:41:18,485
[SPEAKER_02]: Not any thought.

564
00:41:18,545 --> 00:41:19,586
[SPEAKER_02]: Not any agreeable thought.

565
00:41:20,026 --> 00:41:22,447
[SPEAKER_02]: Just a thought pertaining to the pleasure based upon body.

566
00:41:22,468 --> 00:41:29,652
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't want to become neurotic about it either, in the sense of, like, nothing agreeable I must accept.

567
00:41:29,692 --> 00:41:31,133
[SPEAKER_02]: And everything is dangerous.

568
00:41:31,153 --> 00:41:31,373
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

569
00:41:32,253 --> 00:41:33,194
[SPEAKER_02]: There are wholesome things out there.

570
00:41:34,370 --> 00:41:53,837
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, if the mind is not thinking, not thinking any sensual things, and is at the same time withdrawing itself from being sort of liable to the touch or the possibility of the sensual things, basically.

571
00:41:53,857 --> 00:41:57,638
[SPEAKER_02]: I mean, it cannot be touched by the possibilities either, even if they are arising.

572
00:41:58,578 --> 00:42:03,340
[SPEAKER_02]: Even on the level of mind, a thought of pleasure doesn't pull the mind towards that pleasure.

573
00:42:04,503 --> 00:42:04,963
[SPEAKER_02]: That's fine.

574
00:42:05,003 --> 00:42:06,424
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't have to keep pressing it further.

575
00:42:06,564 --> 00:42:07,104
[SPEAKER_02]: Keep it there.

576
00:42:08,204 --> 00:42:09,104
[SPEAKER_02]: This turn was there.

577
00:42:09,844 --> 00:42:10,645
[SPEAKER_02]: Set it there.

578
00:42:11,405 --> 00:42:12,585
[SPEAKER_02]: That's actually first jhāna.

579
00:42:15,726 --> 00:42:31,630
[SPEAKER_02]: So, when I say the surmounting, the possibilities of sensual pleasure, that's what the suttas, when they talk about preventing the unarisen, unwholesome states from arising.

580
00:42:32,218 --> 00:42:35,499
[SPEAKER_02]: You prevent them by not delighting in the possibility of them.

581
00:42:36,160 --> 00:42:47,344
[SPEAKER_02]: Basically, un-arisen, unwholesome states are the possibilities of the sensuality, which is unwholesome, are the possibilities of unwholesome, be it sensuality or will.

582
00:42:48,064 --> 00:42:52,186
[SPEAKER_02]: So, un-arisen, unwholesome equals possibility of unwholesome.

583
00:42:53,226 --> 00:42:57,228
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's where you basically, on that level, you free your mind from it.

584
00:42:58,309 --> 00:43:01,690
[SPEAKER_02]: And if the mind is free on the level of the un-arisen states,

585
00:43:02,411 --> 00:43:10,433
[SPEAKER_02]: of the unwholesome nature, then the mind cannot be controlled, touched, or engaged with the states that are actual, right in front of you, arisen.

586
00:43:12,593 --> 00:43:19,735
[SPEAKER_01]: The maintenance of wholesome states, isn't it?

587
00:43:19,835 --> 00:43:23,756
[SPEAKER_02]: Again, it's again, it's in regards to the unarisen wholesome states.

588
00:43:23,796 --> 00:43:26,856
[SPEAKER_02]: Possibility of the wholesome states, that's what you train in regard to.

589
00:43:27,656 --> 00:43:29,937
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's how you maintain the actual arisen wholesome states.

590
00:43:31,913 --> 00:43:35,574
[SPEAKER_01]: There's seen a danger, seeing the...

591
00:43:35,614 --> 00:43:36,974
[SPEAKER_01]: Please say gratification.

592
00:43:37,595 --> 00:43:43,736
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, seeing the danger in being liable to the arising of the unwholesome states, of unwholesome nature.

593
00:43:48,638 --> 00:43:51,899
[SPEAKER_02]: Seeing the danger in the possibility of unwholesome affecting you.

594
00:43:52,619 --> 00:43:56,380
[SPEAKER_02]: You see the gratification in the... Sure, in the unwholesome world.

595
00:43:56,680 --> 00:43:56,920
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

596
00:43:57,240 --> 00:44:00,341
[SPEAKER_02]: You know, would you be delighting in the possibility of unwholesome?

597
00:44:01,461 --> 00:44:02,401
[SPEAKER_02]: Delighting?

598
00:44:02,421 --> 00:44:03,582
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, not in a sensual manner.

599
00:44:03,722 --> 00:44:09,984
[SPEAKER_02]: In order to welcome and... Well, not delighting, it's the also... Yeah, exactly, yeah.

600
00:44:10,925 --> 00:44:13,566
[SPEAKER_02]: You might want it, but that wanting will be on the level of wisdom.

601
00:44:13,906 --> 00:44:18,427
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, wanting, recognizing, this is liberation, this is the freedom, this is the escape.

602
00:44:19,028 --> 00:44:19,568
[SPEAKER_02]: Chanda.

603
00:44:20,268 --> 00:44:21,248
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, exactly.

604
00:44:21,268 --> 00:44:22,209
[SPEAKER_02]: It can go both ways.

